{"id":"kirjath-jearim","name":"Kirjath-Jearim","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:kirjath-jearim"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Kirjath-jearim","text":"City of jaars; i.e., of woods or forests, a Gibeonite town (Josh. 9:17) on the border of Benjamin, to which tribe it was assigned (18:15, 28). The ark was brought to this place (1 Sam. 7:1, 2) from Beth-shemesh and put in charge of Abinadab, a Levite. Here it remained till it was removed by David to Jerusalem (2 Sam. 6:2, 3, 12; 1 Chr. 15:1-29; comp. Ps. 132). It was also called Baalah (Josh. 15:9) and Kirjath-baal (60). It has been usually identified with Kuriet el-‘Enab (i.e., “city of grapes”), among the hills, about 8 miles north-east of ‘Ain Shems (i.e., Beth-shemesh). The opinion, however, that it is to be identified with ‘Erma, 4 miles east of ‘Ain Shems, on the edge of the valley of Sorek, seems to be better supported. (See KIRJATH.) The words of Ps. 132:6, “We found it in the fields of the wood,” refer to the sojourn of the ark at Kirjath-jearim. “Wood” is here the rendering of …"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H7157","lemma":"קִרְיַת יְעָרִים","xlit":"Qiryath Yᵉʻârîym","gloss":"Kirjath-Jearim or Kirjath-Arim, a place in Palestine","kjv":"Kirjath, Kirjath-jearim, Kirjath-arim","count":13,"share":0.5},{"strong":"H727","lemma":"אָרוֹן","xlit":"ʼârôwn","gloss":"a box","kjv":"ark, chest, coffin","count":15,"share":0.58},{"strong":"H5798","lemma":"עֻזָּא","xlit":"ʻUzzâʼ","gloss":"Uzza or Uzzah, the name of five Israelites","kjv":"Uzza, Uzzah","count":5,"share":0.19},{"strong":"H41","lemma":"אֲבִינָדָב","xlit":"ʼĂbîynâdâb","gloss":"Abinadab, the name of four Israelites","kjv":"Abinadab","count":4,"share":0.15},{"strong":"H3716","lemma":"כְּפִירָה","xlit":"Kᵉphîyrâh","gloss":"Kephirah, a place in Palestine","kjv":"Chephirah","count":3,"share":0.12},{"strong":"H881","lemma":"בְּאֵרוֹת","xlit":"Bᵉʼêrôwth","gloss":"Beeroth, a place in Palestine","kjv":"Beeroth","count":3,"share":0.1